<%- include('../partials/head', { title, description, pagePath }) %>
<div class="info-page info-modern partnerships-page"><%- include('../partials/nav') %>
<main class="info-main container">
  <p class="eyebrow">Crowdwide / Partnerships</p>
  <h1>Grow together, openly.</h1>
  <p class="info-intro">Run a website, a community, a school, a publication or a business? Become a Crowdwide partner: you may show the Crowdwide name and logo on your site, and we show your name and logo on ours.</p>
  <p class="partner-cta-row">
    <a class="button button-primary" href="/partnerships/apply">Apply to partner <span class="btn-arrow"><%- icon('arrow-up-right', { size: 14 }) %></span></a>
    <a class="button button-ghost" href="/partnerships/terms">Read the Partnership Terms</a>
  </p>

  <div class="info-sections partner-benefits">
    <article><span class="principle-number">01</span><h2>Display Crowdwide</h2><p>Approved partners may show the Crowdwide name and logo on their website to say they partner with us, following the <a href="/partnerships/brand-guidelines">Partner Brand Guidelines</a>. A ready-to-use brand kit is included.</p></article>
    <article><span class="principle-number">02</span><h2>Be shown on Crowdwide</h2><p>Your name, logo and website link appear in the partner sections of the Crowdwide home page, footer and about page, wherever partners are listed.</p></article>
    <article><span class="principle-number">03</span><h2>Free and fair</h2><p>There is no fee, no exclusivity and no sharing of member data. Either side can end the partnership at any time. Partnership is not an endorsement.</p></article>
  </div>

  <section class="partner-process" aria-labelledby="process-heading">
    <h2 id="process-heading">How it works</h2>
    <ol class="partner-steps">
      <li><strong>Apply.</strong> Send the short form with your organization, website and contact details, and confirm you have the rights to your name and logo.</li>
      <li><strong>Review.</strong> A Crowdwide administrator checks your website and request. We may contact you for more detail. You get an email with the decision.</li>
      <li><strong>Get listed.</strong> If approved, we add your logo, name and website to the partner sections, and you may display the Crowdwide brand on your site.</li>
      <li><strong>Stay in good standing.</strong> Follow the Brand Guidelines and Terms. Either side may end the partnership at any time, and we remove the listing promptly.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="partner-process" aria-labelledby="fit-heading">
    <h2 id="fit-heading">Who can apply</h2>
    <p>Businesses, non-profits, educational institutions, communities, media outlets, creators and developers that own or control a public website and are lawfully allowed to partner. We do not partner with websites that promote adult or sexually explicit content, gambling or betting, illegal goods or services, hate, harassment, fraud, malware or deceptive practices, or that infringe others' rights. Applying does not guarantee approval, and we may decline a request without detailed explanation beyond the reason we send you.</p>
  </section>

  <%- include('../partials/partners-strip', { variant: 'inline' }) %>

  <section class="partner-process" aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
    <h2 id="faq-heading">Common questions</h2>
    <details><summary>Does a partnership cost anything?</summary><p>No. Crowdwide does not charge partnership fees, and no money, revenue share, Waves or other consideration changes hands because of a partnership. Advertising on Crowdwide is a separate service under the <a href="/advertising/terms">Advertising Terms</a>.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Does Crowdwide share member data with partners?</summary><p>No. Partnering does not give a partner access to Crowdwide accounts, content or personal data, and we do not receive your visitors' data. See the <a href="/privacy">Privacy policy</a>.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Can I use the Crowdwide logo before I am approved?</summary><p>No. The brand license starts only when your request is approved and ends when the partnership ends. Until then please do not imply any partnership.</p></details>
    <details><summary>How do I end a partnership or change my listing?</summary><p>Email <a href="mailto:developerpuneet2010@gmail.com">developerpuneet2010@gmail.com</a> with your reference number. We remove or update a listing promptly, and you remove the Crowdwide brand from your site within 14 days.</p></details>
    <details><summary>What happens to the information I submit?</summary><p>It is used only to review and manage your request, kept while the partnership is active, and deleted 180 days after a rejection or the end of a partnership. See the <a href="/privacy">Privacy policy</a>.</p></details>
  </section>

  <p class="partner-cta-row"><a class="button button-primary" href="/partnerships/apply">Start your application <span class="btn-arrow"><%- icon('arrow-up-right', { size: 14 }) %></span></a>
    <a class="button button-ghost" href="/partnerships/brand-guidelines">Brand guidelines</a></p>
</main>
<%- include('../partials/site-footer') %></div>
<%- include('../partials/foot') %>
